{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123472","id":4520907844,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDXeURA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123472","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123472.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123472.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123472","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123472/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123472/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123472/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bf3a9a333b564145a9a4b945beaac3b6a0ff9a97","number":123472,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Use narrowed types from `is` type checks in `if` blocks","user":{"login":"Adarsh-Me","id":122873385,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1LmKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122873385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me","html_url":"https://github.com/Adarsh-Me","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\nWhen `debug/gdscript/warnings/unsafe_property_access` and `debug/gdscript/warnings/unsafe_method_access` are set to warning or error, accessing a member on a variable that was just checked with `is` still reports the warning, even though the check proves the access is safe:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc foo(reward: Reward) -> void:\r\n\tif reward is GoldReward:\r\n\t\tprint(reward.value) # UNSAFE_PROPERTY_ACCESS, even though it was just checked.\r\n\t\tprint(reward.calc()) # UNSAFE_METHOD_ACCESS.\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Approach\r\n\r\nThe analyzer now tracks a narrowed type for variables that are tested with `is` type tests in the condition of an `if` statement (including the operands of an `and` in that condition):\r\n\r\n- While the `true` block of that statement is being resolved, occurrences of the checked variable use the tested type instead of its declared type. Since the narrowed type is a hard type, the member access resolves statically and the unsafe access warnings no longer fire.\r\n- Only local variables, static variables, and function parameters can be narrowed. Identifiers are matched against their source node, so a shadowing declaration in the block (e.g. a `for` loop variable with the same name) is not affected.\r\n- If the variable is assigned inside the block, the narrowed type is invalidated from that point on, since it may then hold a value of another type. Code before the assignment still benefits from the narrowing, matching the execution order.\r\n- This applies to `Variant` variables as well, which is the most common case where the unsafe warnings fire on `is`-checked values.\r\n\r\nCompletions already partially understand `is` narrowing (see #120492), but this PR makes the analyzer itself aware of it, which is what drives the warnings.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/analyzer/features/is_type_narrowing.gd`: reproduces the issue scenario and checks the code both analyzes and runs correctly.\r\n- `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/analyzer/warnings/type_narrowing.gd`: checks that unsafe access warnings are no longer emitted after an `is` check, that they still fire outside the narrowed block, and that an assignment inside the block invalidates the narrowing.\r\n\r\nAll file-based GDScript tests (512) pass, including the binary tokens variant on Linux CI.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-13T21:09:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T12:01:25Z","closed_at":"2026-09-14T10:15:20Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7cc8ef8aeb0ba932b31e3581d475245098363305","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Adarsh-Me:gdscript-narrow-is-check","ref":"gdscript-narrow-is-check","repo":{"id":1368862654,"node_id":"R_kgDOUZcvvg","name":"godot","full_name":"Adarsh-Me/godot","owner":{"login":"Adarsh-Me","id":122873385,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1LmKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122873385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me","html_url":"https://github.com/Adarsh-Me","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adarsh-Me/repos","events_url":"https://